" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7dc79012-37fe-53ec-a095-ee15868c4f49" :question/math-academy-id "q-279493" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ If $f(X)={X}^{2}+1$, find $f(A).$\n\n| $f(A)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+1 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(A)={A}^{2}+I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & ={A}^{2}+I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+1 & 0+0 \\\\ 0+0 & -1+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284425 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddaa81b6-67eb-521a-b24c-0eeca1554dba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284427} {:answer/id #uuid "d1d8b520-e231-5243-9511-01de95332e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1d8b