37dfeab-e27d-5728-9d16-79567dd4af9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-279495" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $H=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ If $f(X)={X}^{2}+3X+2$, find $f(H).$\n\n| $f(H)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+3X+2 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+3X+2I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(H)={H}^{2}+3H+2I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${H}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{2} & =H\\cdot H \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(H):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(H) & ={H}^{2}+3H+2I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}9 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7+9+2 & -3+(-3)+0 \\\\ 6+6+0 & -2+0+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}18 & -6 \\\\ 12 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284435 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "023c04cc-305f-5ebd-86f7-133b6333c63b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284437} {:answer/id #uuid "76a435c6-5997-5d40-aa02-99b267412c1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid