uid "23ecebe1-0f93-54cc-904f-4a3be5a3b398" :question/math-academy-id "q-279512" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ If $f(X)={X}^{2}-2X-3$, find $f(A).$\n\n| $f(A)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-2X-3 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-2X-3I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(A)={A}^{2}-2A-3I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14 & -10 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & ={A}^{2}-2A-3I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14 & -10 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14 & -10 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14-8-3 & -10-(-4)-0 \\\\ 5-2-0 & -1-2-3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115866 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4fb7cc3-5aeb-5ddd-9cf0-3fbab6033d7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114568} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d25a78-6b54-59db-90df-948b54af3500" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114569} {:answer/id #uuid "cf970816-aec0-5610-a43e-00df25333991" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114570} {:answer/id #uuid "f46792ee-ff3c-5468-81ed-e3218f26d4b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114571} {:answer/id #uuid "68fcda54-07b2-5a9e-a8e0-7d8b8c557e11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9d25a78-6b54-59db-90df-948b54af3500" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114569} :answer-field/id #uuid "75539ef4-3ad6-5964-bced-905551f374c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114567}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "12dbb97a-a553-543b-a68a-7b1edc9cc29f" :question/math-academy-id "q-78348" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find $f(C)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-2X-5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-2X-5 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-2X-5I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(C)={C}^{2}-2C-5I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${C}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(C):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(C) & ={C}^{2}-2C-5I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]-5[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7-2-5 & 4-4-0 \\\\ 6-6-0 & 7-2-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e970fe-cff8-50e3-9b94-67ad97b03da7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f946525-3e2d-5abf-8f4f-ade88c6a78e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 12 \\\\ 14 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284447} {:answer/id #uuid "983c14d0-0db6-5203-bfe1-99c5b48dca63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284448} {:answer/id #uuid "698b32d9-6289-5b45-bcdc-a2c9e01f4e22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 19\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284449} {:answer/id #uuid "d9055baf-fb78-52f6-87c5-7fa9a4f63ffc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 12 \\\\ 1 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284450} {:answer/id #uuid "3596a79d-183e-540f-9d7a-11e50b3beb07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 19\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3596a79d-183e-540f-9d7a-11e50b3beb07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 19\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284451} :answer-field/id #uuid "a62ee48d-d3b9-5811-ba8d-1cd397e60b60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "88934d15-ae66-5c80-a236-6a63bba3d33b" :question/math-academy-id "q-78497" :question/problem "If $F=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]$, then ${F}^{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${F}^{2},$ we multiply $F$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{2} & =F\\cdot F \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 19\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e970fe-cff8-50e3-9b94-67ad97b03da7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06745842-85c5-5a45-99fc-d014e371e25d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 18 \\\\ 38 & 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284454} {:answer/id #uuid "c16b8cba-5791-533e-a4df-cdc2cb5c8351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284455} {:answer/id #uuid "a99315ae-593d-5a8a-b744-0d3abd9648a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284456} {:answer/id #uuid "8c8f76a0-af9d-5cd1-908e-dfab76396ef6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}38 & 18 \\\\ 9 & 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284457} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf691f3-11c6-541e-8231-04849a2d42bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}38 & 11 \\\\ 9 & 18\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c8f76a0-af9d-5cd1-908e-dfab76396ef6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}38 & 18 \\\\ 9 & 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284457} :answer-field/id #uuid "f09617f4-da7c-5ef8-868f-474acd771b45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a716a0dd-bb51-5dc9-aa66-cfc859ba3d36" :question/math-academy-id "q-78528" :question/problem "If $Z=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$, then ${Z}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, to find ${Z}^{2},$ we multiply $Z$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Z}^{2} & =Z\\cdot Z \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${Z}^{4}={Z}^{2}\\cdot {Z}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Z}^{4} & ={Z}^{2}\\cdot {Z}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}38 & 18 \\\\ 9 & 11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e970fe-cff8-50e3-9b94-67ad97b03da7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4abee4ce-ae74-5f6e-b252-b1aada71deaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284461} {:answer/id #uuid "9da8218a-eb9f-5275-a319-2147643d2629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284462} {:answer/id #uuid "4f5923c5-a98d-5bb9-8269-4d43a37fc77b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\